WEBVTT

00:29:58.311 --> 00:30:00.335
AG: Yeah, I guess that goes
to the question

00:30:00.359 --> 00:30:02.380
of narcissistic leadership.

00:30:02.404 --> 00:30:05.659
And I know you know
I've spent a lot of my career

00:30:05.683 --> 00:30:07.834
studying the dynamics
of giving and taking,

00:30:07.858 --> 00:30:14.049
and in the IPO there's just
an unusual number of "Is" and "mes",

00:30:14.073 --> 00:30:17.198
and we know from evidence
that narcissistic taker CEOs

00:30:17.222 --> 00:30:18.941
are more likely to use "I" and "me"

00:30:18.965 --> 00:30:20.826
when talking about their companies.

00:30:21.310 --> 00:30:27.174
There's one article calling Adam
the most talented grifter of our time.

00:30:27.499 --> 00:30:31.105
I'm just curious to hear your reaction
to that set of observations.